# Kaggle API credentials -- almost certainly NOT needed.
#
# All four datasets currently download without an account. This file exists only
# as a fallback in case Kaggle starts requiring auth for the Twitter dataset; the
# download script will tell you if that happens.
#
# If it does:
#   1. python3 scripts/download_data.py --init-env   # copies this file to .env
#   2. Sign in at https://www.kaggle.com
#   3. https://www.kaggle.com/settings -> "API" -> "Create New Token"
#      A kaggle.json downloads. Open it in any text editor:
#        {"username":"janedoe","key":"a1b2c3d4e5f6..."}
#   4. Paste both values into .env (this file is only the template).
#   5. python3 scripts/download_data.py --all
#
# .env is gitignored, so your key cannot be committed by accident.
# Never put real credentials in this file -- .env.example IS committed.

KAGGLE_USERNAME=
KAGGLE_KEY=
